From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:46:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iio: light: tsl2583: Clamp CT819 lux like iOS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AppleCT819 computes lux from the counts (_calculateAmbient, iOS
0xfffffff005bc6a60) and clamps it to 5000, which it also publishes as
ALSSensorMax. A channel at the ADC limit, 1024 counts per 2.7 ms
integration cycle minus one, is clipped and its ratio meaningless, so
such a reading reports the maximum too.

Move the lux computation into tsl2583.h as apple_als_calc_lux() with
the per-cycle count limit and the largest reported value as
parameters, and describe the CT819 values in its match data. The CT821
keeps its 16-bit limit and 65535 maximum. Add KUnit cases for the lux
curve, integration time, gain, dark counts and saturation.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux e846959b (J71t ledger 9.2); unchanged in
 substance.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
